Ship the Help patch in the installed library.

Upstream ships libdir-help.pd in the tarball but does not list it in the
Makefile's `datafiles`, so `make install` leaves the help patch behind even
though libdir-meta.pd -- the file this library exists to ship -- is what makes
Pd's Help Browser pick the library up in the first place.  Add it to the
install set so a dropped-in libdir is self-contained.

Pure build-system change: no platform macro, no source code touched.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -16,7 +16,8 @@
 TODO.txt \
 LICENSE.txt \
 README.txt \
-libdir-meta.pd
+libdir-meta.pd \
+libdir-help.pd

 datadirs =

 cflags = -DVERSION='"$(lib.version)"'
